@format 1
@id media-preview.common.viewer-close
@title Viewer close
@section Media preview
@area Common
@entry unload-button, removed-loaded-path, workspace-clear
@summary Trace every currently reachable PViewerMediaClose trigger through its close gate, backend LMediaUnload publication, viewer ownership invalidation, committed-state clearing, and empty viewer-media publication.
@related media-preview.common.backend-load, media-preview.common.completion-routing, media-preview.common.media-publication, media-removal.common.docket-removal, media-removal.common.workspace-media-clear
@tag media
@tag preview
@tag common
@tag unload
@tag viewer

@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad
@alias surface = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PTabSurface
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace

[unload-button] Viewer Unload button Click <input>
~ This starts with viewer Unload button Click.
[Technical explanation]
- The close button built by PViewerCloseBuild calls PViewerMediaClose with its default force=false @ viewer.PViewerCloseBuild(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> close-request-join

[removed-loaded-path] Loaded path removed from a tab Files list <input>
~ This starts with loaded path removed from a tab Files list.
[Technical explanation]
- PTabViewerAttach reacts to PListClearChange; if the removed paths contain the viewer's committed source, it calls PViewerMediaClose(force=true) before clearing the flow @ surface.PTabViewerAttach(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> close-request-join

[workspace-clear] Workspace media clear <input>
~ This starts with workspace media clear.
[Technical explanation]
- PWorkspaceMediaClear calls PViewerMediaClose(force=true) when the workspace has a viewer @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> close-request-join

[close-request-join] Close requests converge <junction>
> close-gate

[close-gate] Viewer close gate <decision>
~ The program checks whether the preview panel is allowed to close the current media.
[Technical explanation]
- Reject an unloaded viewer; also reject a non-forced close while viewer commands are inactive @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
? "Viewer may close" > backend-unload
? "Unloaded, or inactive without force" > close-rejected

[backend-unload] Backend unload attempt <decision>
~ The background media loader tries to clear its current media state.
[Technical explanation]
- LMediaUnload checks whether backend loading is pending or backend current path/info exists; when changed, it cancels the current request, advances backend generation, clears backend state, creates an Unloaded outcome, and raises LMediaLoadCompleted synchronously @ media-load.LMediaUnload(...)
? "Backend state changed" > backend-unload-raised
? "Backend already empty" > backend-empty-check

[close-rejected] Close rejected <output>
~ This path ends with close rejected.
[Technical explanation]
= PViewerMediaClose returns false without changing backend or committed viewer state.

[backend-unload-raised] Backend Unloaded outcome reaches viewer subscriber <process>
~ The background loader reports that the media was unloaded.
[Technical explanation]
- LMediaLoadRaise invokes each completion subscriber individually; PViewerLoadHandle receives the Unloaded outcome and queues a dispatcher callback using the viewer load serial that is current at this moment @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
! This backend event occurs before PViewerMediaClose advances pViewerLoadSerial or clears pViewerLoadPath.
> backend-changed-align

[backend-empty-check] Committed viewer state exists <decision>
~ The program checks whether the preview panel still has current media state.
[Technical explanation]
- When LMediaUnload reports no backend change, PViewerMediaClose continues only if PViewerSourcePath or viewer media information still records committed viewer state @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
? "Committed viewer state exists" > backend-empty-align
? "Backend and viewer already empty" > already-empty

[backend-changed-align] Backend-changed path alignment <junction>
> close-state-join

[backend-empty-align] Backend-empty path alignment <junction>
> close-state-join

[already-empty] Viewer already empty <output>
~ The preview panel already has no media to close.
[Technical explanation]
= PViewerMediaClose returns false because neither backend state nor committed viewer media state required closing.

[close-state-join] Closable viewer paths converge <junction>
> viewer-close-state

[viewer-close-state] Invalidate viewer load and clear committed media <process>
~ The preview forgets the old loading request and clears the current media.
[Technical explanation]
- Advance pViewerLoadSerial, clear the expected load path, hide preview, dispose player state, clear PViewerSourcePath/media/crop, reset stopped playback state, and apply the empty preview state @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
> viewer-publish

[viewer-publish] Publish empty viewer media cargo <process>
~ The preview panel announces that it no longer has media loaded.
[Technical explanation]
- Log the close and synchronously raise an empty LCargo through PViewerMediaRaise @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
  @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
> queued-backend-check

[queued-backend-check] Queued backend Unloaded callback <decision>
~ The program checks whether an earlier background unload notice is still waiting to run.
[Technical explanation]
- If LMediaUnload raised an outcome, its queued PViewerLoadHandle callback later rechecks viewer lifetime, the captured load serial, and expected path; the close has advanced the serial and cleared the expected path, so that backend Unloaded callback is stale @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
? "Backend Unloaded callback was queued" > stale-backend-callback
? "No backend callback was queued" > no-backend-align

[stale-backend-callback] Backend Unloaded callback ignored <process>
~ This step handles background loader Unloaded follow-up notice ignored.
[Technical explanation]
- Return from the dispatcher callback without publishing a second viewer-media failure/empty cargo because its ownership/path checks no longer match @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
> close-join

[no-backend-align] No backend callback remains <junction>
> close-join

[close-join] Viewer-close paths converge <junction>
> closed

[closed] Viewer closed <output>
~ This path ends with viewer closed.
[Technical explanation]
= PViewerMediaClose returns true after committed viewer state is emptied and its own empty viewer-media cargo is published; any backend Unloaded completion queued earlier is prevented from reapplying by the viewer ownership/path checks.
